"He looks at your face and struggles to focus. ""You are not with the Commonwealth Guard! Wh..where are our reinforcements?""

The man clenches his jaw and squeezes his eyes shut. In this moment he seems to realize that whatever reinforcements he was expecting is not coming.

He opens his eyes again and looks up at you. ""You must leave. This place is crawling with Goblins. If you make it to Bastion Spire you need to tell them that our attempt to reclaim Grimmhold has failed. The gates remain closed and Grimmhold is not passable.""",
"""Is there any way to make Grimmhold passable again?""�",
"""Perhaps, but you can't do it on your own. <cough> The Goblins destroyed the lever that retracts the gates barricading the Eastern Gap. The only way to open the gates now is to activate the secondary water gate beneath Grimmhold which will...<cough>...will force the gates open. But they infest that area as well. We tried to clear them out but their numbers were too great.""

The man's eyes seem to fill with despair. ""You'll need to take the northern route west.""",
"""I'm going to open this water gate and take back Grimmhold myself. Goblins be damned!""*",
"""Don't be a fool! Six of my Guardsmen couldn't accomplish this feat...I...[cough]""

With that last cough, the soldier appears to lack the strength needed for another breath. He gasps and shakes as blood spurts from his mouth. As his eyes roll back into his head, his body goes limp.

He is at rest.",
